{"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingYourFirstApp"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation"},{"title":"Explanation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Explanation"}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"article","metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Design Principles","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux’s surface area looks small — a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a reducer protocol, a plugin protocol — but the API is opinionated. These principles explain ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"why","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the API has the shape it does, so you can extend it correctly."}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"1-State-is-a-value-observation-is-a-class","type":"heading","text":"1. State is a value, observation is a class"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"State is a struct. Mutations go through ","type":"text"},{"code":"inout State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which is predictable, snapshottable, and testable. SwiftUI observation needs an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" reference type. Reconciling these two requires a class that mirrors the struct."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" generates that class for you ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<StructName>Observer"},{"type":"text","text":") and wires up the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance that bridges the two. Don’t hand-write the observer. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pack → reduce → unpack-diff → observe"},{"type":"text","text":" cycle is what gives you per-property re-renders without coupling reducers to a class."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Slice"},{"type":"text","text":" extends this to nested struct slices: each slice gets its own observer class so observation stays granular even across composition."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"2. Reducers are pure and synchronous","anchor":"2-Reducers-are-pure-and-synchronous"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reducers take "},{"code":"inout State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and an "},{"code":"Action","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", mutate state in place, and return an optional "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect"},{"text":". They never ","type":"text"},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", never ","type":"text"},{"code":"throw","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and never call I\/O directly.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Why: pure synchronous mutations are trivially testable, deterministic, and snapshot-friendly. When you need async work (network, disk, timers), return an effect — a ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" async closure that runs off the MainActor and dispatches follow-up actions back through ","type":"text"},{"code":"send","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"3. Effects run off MainActor; sends hop back","level":2,"anchor":"3-Effects-run-off-MainActor-sends-hop-back"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","isActive":true},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Sendable (Send) async -> Void","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"text":" runs effects in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task { @concurrent in }"},{"type":"text","text":" so they don’t block UI. "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Send","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"@MainActor @Sendable (Action) -> Void","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so dispatching from inside an effect always lands back on MainActor — no manual hops, no race conditions on state.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The split is deliberate: effects own the work, the reducer owns the state.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"4. Persistence is invisible","level":2,"anchor":"4-Persistence-is-invisible"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reducers mutate "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" properties; "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" records every change in a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" debounces and drains those changesets through "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" closures."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You never write "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"db.save()"},{"type":"text","text":" in a feature. A reducer that adds an item is identical whether the entity is persisted to SwiftData, SQLite, or nowhere — register or don’t register a writer. This is the principle that makes Swidux apps feel small: persistence stops being a concern of feature code."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"5. Synchronous state, async persistence","level":2,"anchor":"5-Synchronous-state-async-persistence"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State updates synchronously inside the reducer for instant UI feedback. Persistence happens asynchronously: "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" change tracking is in-memory and free; the debounced persistence flush coalesces rapid mutations into a single batched write.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tap-tap-tap-tap on an increment button updates the UI on every tap and produces one DB write a moment later. Reducers stay synchronous; storage stays cheap."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"6. Plugins are the single extension point","anchor":"6-Plugins-are-the-single-extension-point","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything that hangs off the dispatch cycle is a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":". Persistence, undo, killswitch, parental gate, paywall — same protocol, same lifecycle hooks. You can add your own without forking Swidux."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two structural patterns:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core middleware"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":") — action-agnostic. Doesn’t know your action type. Couples only to state shape (","type":"text"},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for undo; ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" keypaths for persistence).","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Domain plugins"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"code":"KillswitchPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ParentalGatePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":", your own) — owns a state slice and an action enum. Wires into your root types via keypath + action lifter + extractor."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The decision rule: "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"does this need to know your action type?"}]},{"text":" If no, write core middleware and use ","type":"text"},{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". If yes, write a domain plugin and use ","type":"text"},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"7. Bind to the store, not to `@State`","anchor":"7-Bind-to-the-store-not-to-State","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Form inputs read from the store and dispatch on write. Use ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/binding(_:sending:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" for the common case (read one property, dispatch one action), and fall back to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Binding(get:set:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when the read is a transformation (optional unwraps, derived values) or the setter wraps the dispatch in animation or branching. Don’t buffer mutable form state in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" and write back on a button."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Why: every mutation flows through the reducer, which means undo\/redo, persistence, and any plugin that watches the dispatch cycle sees every keystroke (subject to coalescing). If you stash state in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":", those plugins are blind to it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The trade-off is more dispatches per keystroke. Coalescing — see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — collapses bursts of the same action into a single undo step."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"8. Registration order matters at the boundaries","level":2,"anchor":"8-Registration-order-matters-at-the-boundaries"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" snapshots in "},{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so it must run ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"before","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" any plugin or reducer mutates state — register it first. "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" drains changelogs in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":", so it wants the post-mutation state — register it after undo. Domain plugins use only "},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so their relative order rarely matters.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The recommended order:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. snapshots first","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. drains after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. domain plugins","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)","plugins.register(parentalGatePlugin)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"text":"9. Strict concurrency, on purpose","anchor":"9-Strict-concurrency-on-purpose","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux is built for "},{"code":"swiftLanguageMode(.v6)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and assumes Swift 6 strict concurrency throughout. State must be ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The macros mark generated code carefully. Effects use explicit isolation (","type":"text"},{"code":"@Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"@MainActor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"@concurrent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This is friction at first — you’ll get warnings about ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" types. Honour them. The result is a state-management layer that composes safely with ","type":"text"},{"code":"async\/await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and SwiftData without the surprise data races you get from pre-Swift 6 designs.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"10. The store is opinionated; your app is not","anchor":"10-The-store-is-opinionated-your-app-is-not","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux gives you a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a reducer protocol, a plugin protocol, and three optional plugins. It does not give you:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A dependency-injection container (write your own ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppEnvironment","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A navigation library (use SwiftUI navigation).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A network layer (use ","type":"text"},{"code":"URLSession","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", structured concurrency, or whatever you want).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An opinion on database (SwiftData, GRDB, SQLite, Core Data — register a ","type":"text"},{"code":"StateWriter","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and Swidux doesn’t care).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The store owns one job: take an action, produce a new state, run effects. Everything else is yours.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"11. Service shapes: protocol when others implement it, closures when we own it","anchor":"11-Service-shapes-protocol-when-others-implement-it-closures-when-we-own-it","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux services deliberately come in two shapes, chosen by who supplies the implementation:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Protocol"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — when apps or vendor adapters implement the backend:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (RevenueCat, StoreKit, simulated), ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(Mixpanel, Amplitude, console), ","type":"text"},{"code":"FeatureFlagsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (any JSON host).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A protocol gives conformers a stable, documented contract.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Struct of closures"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — when the library owns the shape and apps only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"configure or mock it: ","type":"text"},{"code":"KillswitchService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"ParentalChallengeSource","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"SyncPreflightService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Closures make the built-in ","type":"text"},{"code":".live","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":".mock","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"factories and per-test overrides trivial without a conformance ceremony.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The split is a signal, not an accident: if you find yourself conforming to a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"struct-of-closures service, that service was designed to be configured, not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"replaced.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Anti-patterns","anchor":"Anti-patterns","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ ","type":"text"},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"try","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" inside a reducer — return an effect instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Hand-writing the observer class when you could use ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Calling ","type":"text"},{"code":"db.save()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from inside a reducer — use ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Mutating state from inside an effect — effects dispatch actions; the reducer mutates.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Owning the store with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@StateObject","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — use ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", not ","type":"text"},{"code":"ObservableObject","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Buffering form state in ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and committing on submit — bind to the store directly.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Registering ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" before ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" — snapshot must precede mutation.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"],["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginArchitecture":{"title":"Plugin Architecture","abstract":[{"text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Send":{"title":"Send","abstract":[{"text":"A function for dispatching actions back to the store from within an effect.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Send","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Send","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/send","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Send","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Effect":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/effect","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Effect"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Effect"}],"title":"Effect","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An async unit of work returned by a reducer."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/StateWriter":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/statewriter","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"StateWriter","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"StateWriter","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"StateWriter","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Accumulates entity snapshots and produces batched async persistence work."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Coalescing persistence plugin."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","title":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistencePlugin"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store/binding(_:sending:)":{"title":"binding(_:sending:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a SwiftUI "},{"code":"Binding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that reads a property through the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"observer tree and dispatches an action when written.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/binding(_:sending:)","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store\/binding(_:sending:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"binding"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"KeyPath","preciseIdentifier":"s:s7KeyPathC"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"State"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Observer","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux0A10ObservableP8ObserverQa"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":">, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"sending"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI7BindingV","text":"Binding","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}]}},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every mutation for downstream persistence."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","title":"EntityStore","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ChangeSet":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tracks which entity IDs have been created\/updated or deleted."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ChangeSet"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/changeset","kind":"symbol","title":"ChangeSet","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ChangeSet"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingYourFirstApp":{"title":"Build Your First Swidux App","abstract":[{"text":"Build a counter app from scratch and meet the four moving parts of a Swidux project: state, action, reducer, and store.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingYourFirstApp","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingyourfirstapp"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"UndoPlugin","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SecurityPosture":{"title":"Security Posture","abstract":[{"text":"What Swidux’s soft controls actually guarantee, and what to do when you need a hard one.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/securityposture"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxPlugin":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxplugin","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A plugin that participates in the Swidux dispatch cycle."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ArchitectureGuide":{"title":"Architecture & Performance","abstract":[{"text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux","role":"collection","title":"Swidux","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}]}}}